/-!
# Exclusions in the radical uniqueness argument

The imported modules construct the C.2.3 setup from characteristic-normalizer
control and eliminate the exceptional-prime and cyclic-automizer alternatives
of 1.3.4. In the surviving binary-block configuration they construct
W = O²(X ∩ K) and X = W Wᵗ. Commuting factors give the actual direct-product
equivalence modulo Z(X). The final action lemmas show how a permuted factor
pair with trace P ∩ K contradicts N_L(P)-irreducibility.

The full noncontainment assertion in 1.3.8 remains unfinished. It still requires
the C.2.7 model exclusions and the application of C.1.9 and Krull–Schmidt,
including the indecomposability and factor-trace hypotheses. No intermediate
contract here asserts those missing results.

Source: Aschbacher–Smith, combined manuscript of 1 March 2004,
proof of Proposition 1.3.8, printed pp.513–514.
-/
